index 0000000..eb8fad7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/wait-no-wait-and-callable-add-4c2e9a7d1f083b65.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+---
+fixes:
+  - |
+    `wait=None`, `wait=0` and `wait=sum([])` mean "no wait" again. They
+    raised `TypeError: 'NoneType' object is not callable` when a retry
+    happened, for both `Retrying` and `AsyncRetrying`.
+  - |
+    Adding a plain callable to a wait strategy, such as
+    `my_callable + wait_fixed(1)`, builds a `wait_combine` that sums both
+    again, instead of raising `TypeError`.
+  - |
+    `wait_combine` passes the retry state to its strategies positionally, so
+    plain callables may use any parameter name.
